The kind lab on 2026-10-26 (UTC), with cub kubara built from the branch that replaces
the server worker with two service accounts. Kubara v0.15.0, cub v0.9.0, ConfigHub
v0.9.5. PREFIX=rh-kubara, KIND=rhk.

Part 1 is run.sh in full. It is the third run on this lab: the first stopped at step 6
on `cub serviceaccount key add --quiet` (that command has no --quiet), and the second
found that on ConfigHub v0.9.2 and later a change order the variants took nothing
from reads Released with nothing published, so four components were never released.
Both are fixed in the branch. So handover.sh below keeps the token and the key the
second run issued.

Part 2 deletes both service accounts and runs handover.sh again: the reinstall case.
Part 3 is handback.sh, after which the token is revoked and the key removed.


