== Done
Every Kubara component now has a base and a variant per cluster in ConfigHub.
To change the platform: edit a base, promote the change stage by stage with
  cub changeorder create ... then cub variant promote and cub variant approve.
Before handover, Kubara's hub delivers from Git; handover points it at approved releases.

== 3. Hand Kubara's hub to ConfigHub

$ cub kubara handover platform --prefix rh-kubara --out confighub --capabilities hub=kind-rhk-hub
Wrote confighub/handover.sh. These ApplicationSets will read ConfigHub instead of Git:
  argocd                   oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/rh-kubara-argo-cd-{{name}}
  cert-manager             oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/rh-kubara-cert-manager-{{name}}
  homer-dashboard          oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/rh-kubara-homer-dashboard-{{name}}
  metrics-server           oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/rh-kubara-metrics-server-{{name}}
  traefik                  oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/rh-kubara-traefik-{{name}}
No ApplicationSet delivers bootstrap-crds, so Kubara's bootstrap keeps it.
Left on Git, for services this platform does not enable: external-dns, external-secrets, kube-prometheus-stack, kyverno, kyverno-policies, kyverno-policy-reporter, loki, longhorn, metallb, oauth2-proxy, reloader, velero
Then it installs argobot v0.2.3 on the hub, which records each release's live status in its variant Space.
It approves each first release as you in: dev, prod.

Next, after apply.sh
  less confighub/handover.sh
  HUB_CONTEXT=<kubectl context of Kubara's hub> bash confighub/handover.sh

$ bash confighub/handover.sh

