Done. Kubara's hub now reads each cluster's approved release from ConfigHub,
and argobot records each Application's sync and health on the release it synced.
See it with: cub release list --space <a variant Space>
Watch it with: kubectl get applications -n argocd
A manual sync must keep RespectIgnoreDifferences, as Kubara's sync options do;
without it, Argo CD empties the values of the Secrets ConfigHub holds without values.

